WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.204 --> 00:00:17.606
&gt;&gt;&gt; The new discovery suggests

00:00:17.739 --> 00:00:19.641
this species may have

00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:22.210
intentionally buried the dead

00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:24.846
and carved symbols off the

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.481
graves of the cave walls before

00:00:26.815 --> 00:00:28.183
burials by modern humans.

00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:29.885
Working in incredibly tight

00:00:30.018 --> 00:00:31.920
spaces in the rising star case

00:00:32.054 --> 00:00:33.722
in South Africa, a team of

00:00:33.855 --> 00:00:35.190
researchers last year made these

00:00:35.324 --> 00:00:37.292
and many other discoveries about

00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:39.628
this ancient species.

00:00:39.761 --> 00:00:42.030
Our next guest is part of that

00:00:42.164 --> 00:00:42.431
expedition.

00:00:42.831 --> 00:00:43.432
He was describing one of the

00:00:43.565 --> 00:00:44.166
engravings after he discovered

00:00:44.299 --> 00:00:48.837
it.

00:00:48.971 --> 00:00:50.138
&gt;&gt; I can't believe what we're

00:00:50.272 --> 00:00:50.839
seeing.

00:00:50.839 --> 00:00:54.843
We're seeing scratch marks, sort

00:00:54.843 --> 00:00:56.111
of, pictures of carvings or

00:00:56.244 --> 00:00:56.845
carving the rock.

00:00:56.845 --> 00:01:00.015
Look at the scale of these

00:01:00.148 --> 00:01:00.349
things.

00:01:00.482 --> 00:01:02.951
&gt;&gt; I'm so happy that we're

00:01:03.085 --> 00:01:06.054
joined by the man you just saw.

00:01:06.188 --> 00:01:07.489
Exploring residence and world

00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:14.229
renowned -- okay, how do I say

00:01:14.363 --> 00:01:15.397
this?

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:15.931
Paleoanthropologist.

00:01:16.064 --> 00:01:16.865
He joins us now.

00:01:16.865 --> 00:01:18.000
He authored it book that comes

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.801
out in August.

00:01:19.935 --> 00:01:20.369
&gt;&gt; August.

00:01:20.502 --> 00:01:22.204
&gt;&gt; "Cave of bones."

00:01:22.337 --> 00:01:24.873
&gt;&gt; I get PTSD looking at that

00:01:24.873 --> 00:01:24.906
image.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.376
&gt;&gt; That is very claustrophobic

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:28.377
to begin with.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.879
&gt;&gt; To get in there, you go down

00:01:30.879 --> 00:01:33.648
about a 40-foot shaft that is --

00:01:33.782 --> 00:01:36.551
gets down to 7 1/2 inches.

00:01:36.885 --> 00:01:37.919
Average is 9 inches.

00:01:38.053 --> 00:01:39.454
&gt;&gt; Absolutely not.

00:01:39.588 --> 00:01:40.355
&gt;&gt; Guess how much weight you

00:01:40.489 --> 00:01:41.456
lost to do it?

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:42.424
&gt;&gt; 55 pounds.

00:01:42.557 --> 00:01:43.825
&gt;&gt; Because you wanted to see

00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:44.259
this so much.

00:01:44.393 --> 00:01:45.861
&gt;&gt; I had to test it.

00:01:45.994 --> 00:01:47.496
We discovered these burials.

00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:49.331
We realized there were burials

00:01:49.464 --> 00:01:52.901
in 2018 on this "National

00:01:53.001 --> 00:01:54.436
geographic" expedition.

00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:55.570
I had only seen this thing

00:01:55.704 --> 00:01:56.338
through video.

00:01:56.471 --> 00:01:58.907
And we had the questions over

00:01:59.041 --> 00:01:59.241
covid.

00:01:59.374 --> 00:02:00.909
And we could not get them

00:02:01.043 --> 00:02:01.276
answered.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:02.277
There are only 47 humans that

00:02:02.411 --> 00:02:09.351
had ever been in there.

00:02:09.484 --> 00:02:10.919
We started making discoveries.

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:12.387
Our missions were focused.

00:02:12.521 --> 00:02:14.923
We saw the symbols.

00:02:14.923 --> 00:02:15.624
It blew my mind.

00:02:15.757 --> 00:02:17.459
&gt;&gt; Do you know what they mean?

00:02:17.592 --> 00:02:18.160
&gt;&gt; No.

00:02:18.293 --> 00:02:19.661
And in essence --

00:02:19.795 --> 00:02:22.531
&gt;&gt; How did you conclude what you

00:02:22.931 --> 00:02:22.998
think they are?

00:02:23.131 --> 00:02:24.266
&gt;&gt; This is not a human species.

00:02:24.399 --> 00:02:25.901
They have a brain the third the

00:02:26.034 --> 00:02:26.601
size of ours.

00:02:26.935 --> 00:02:28.937
It's about the size of a

00:02:28.937 --> 00:02:29.204
chimpanzee.

00:02:29.337 --> 00:02:31.840
And they're carving symbols,

00:02:31.973 --> 00:02:32.941
150,000 before even humans think

00:02:33.041 --> 00:02:33.975
of doing that.

00:02:34.109 --> 00:02:36.278
They look familiar to us.

00:02:36.411 --> 00:02:40.982
Crosses, boxes, triangles, hash

00:02:41.116 --> 00:02:41.349
tags.

00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:42.284
They don't have Twitter.

00:02:42.417 --> 00:02:43.018
&gt;&gt; I know that.

00:02:43.151 --> 00:02:44.519
&gt;&gt; And, yet, we may never know

00:02:44.953 --> 00:02:45.387
what they mean.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.590
They were made for other

00:02:48.957 --> 00:02:49.357
species, not us.

00:02:49.491 --> 00:02:50.492
&gt;&gt; One thing that I know that I

00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:51.760
took away from what I read about

00:02:51.893 --> 00:02:53.095
the work that you've done on

00:02:53.228 --> 00:02:56.965
this is that what you discovered

00:02:56.965 --> 00:03:00.135
erases the belief in human

00:03:00.268 --> 00:03:01.937
conceptionalism because of the

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:02.504
size of our brain.

00:03:02.637 --> 00:03:04.473
&gt;&gt; We told this story since --

00:03:04.606 --> 00:03:05.907
for thousands of years.

00:03:06.041 --> 00:03:06.975
Why are we different?

00:03:06.975 --> 00:03:08.443
We want to make ourselves

00:03:08.577 --> 00:03:08.977
different.

00:03:08.977 --> 00:03:10.979
One of the last things we had is

00:03:11.079 --> 00:03:13.115
this big brain.

00:03:13.248 --> 00:03:17.919
That just died just that with

00:03:18.053 --> 00:03:18.353
this evidence.

00:03:18.487 --> 00:03:19.321
We're not exceptional.

00:03:19.454 --> 00:03:20.122
&gt;&gt; Can you explain that?

00:03:20.255 --> 00:03:20.589
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:22.257
So humans have got this

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.259
narrative that our big brain is

00:03:24.392 --> 00:03:25.026
super charged us.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.628
Made us different.

00:03:26.995 --> 00:03:29.164
Let's do culture and symbols,

00:03:29.297 --> 00:03:30.398
music, art, all the things we

00:03:30.532 --> 00:03:31.500
like to separate ourselves from

00:03:31.633 --> 00:03:33.468
the animal kingdom.

00:03:33.602 --> 00:03:35.003
Animal studies have shown us

00:03:35.003 --> 00:03:36.238
that is not true.

00:03:36.371 --> 00:03:39.107
Whales do incredible things.

00:03:39.241 --> 00:03:41.009
Crows, they're brilliant.

00:03:41.009 --> 00:03:43.011
But now we know that neither

00:03:43.011 --> 00:03:44.346
were we exceptional in our

00:03:44.479 --> 00:03:46.481
brain, the brain doesn't make us

00:03:46.615 --> 00:03:49.918
whatever it is we are.

00:03:50.051 --> 00:03:57.159
We now

00:03:57.292 --> 00:03:57.692
250,000 years ago.

00:03:57.826 --> 00:03:59.327
&gt;&gt; Your energy and passion tells

00:03:59.461 --> 00:04:01.029
me that you are not but any

00:04:01.062 --> 00:04:01.730
means done.

00:04:01.863 --> 00:04:05.600
What's next in terms of your

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:05.967
research?

00:04:06.101 --> 00:04:06.701
&gt;&gt; Firstly, we are bringing this

00:04:07.035 --> 00:04:07.135
to the world.

00:04:07.269 --> 00:04:10.105
We are going to engage the

00:04:10.238 --> 00:04:11.406
entire scientific community how

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.775
to test he's hypotheses.

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:15.043
It's science.

00:04:15.043 --> 00:04:16.011
It's ongoing.

00:04:16.144 --> 00:04:17.712
Also asking the world, what do

00:04:17.846 --> 00:04:23.084
we do with this?

00:04:23.218 --> 00:04:25.053
What do we do with discovering

00:04:25.053 --> 00:04:25.620
the first non-human species that

00:04:25.754 --> 00:04:26.188
had our capabilities?

00:04:26.321 --> 00:04:29.090
This is a special place for

00:04:29.224 --> 00:04:29.691
them.

00:04:29.824 --> 00:04:30.425
They took the dead of their kin

00:04:30.559 --> 00:04:32.360
into remote areas and buried

00:04:32.494 --> 00:04:32.661
them.

00:04:33.061 --> 00:04:35.063
Do we destroy it in the way we

00:04:35.063 --> 00:04:37.432
humans tend to, or do we take

00:04:37.566 --> 00:04:37.832
care here?

00:04:37.966 --> 00:04:39.734
I think it's a special -- it's

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.403
almost our first contact moment,

00:04:41.536 --> 00:04:43.071
the real first contact moment.

00:04:43.205 --> 00:04:44.472
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:04:44.606 --> 00:04:48.276
Paleo anthropologist, Dr. Lee

